@tconley1428 

definitely makes sense. what are your thoughts on adding this custom model provider implementation as an example in the SDK for others? this seems to work for me

(people can implment their own routing logic)

```
class RoutingModelProvider(ModelProvider):
    def __init__(self):
        self.openai_provider = OpenAIProvider(openai_client=AsyncOpenAI(max_retries=0))
        self.litellm_provider = LitellmProvider()

    def get_model(self, model_name: str | None) -> Model:
        # Route to LiteLLM for provider-prefixed models (e.g., "gemini/gemini-2.0-flash")
        if model_name and re.match(r"^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+/", model_name):
            return self.litellm_provider.get_model(model_name)

        return self.openai_provider.get_model(model_name)
```
